      "writtenOn": "2021-02-02T17:35:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Stephen,\n\nCorrect me if I\u0027m wrong, but there\u0027s nothing that prevents doing this into a separated vendor module, is there ? Your thermal and core_ctl drivers could simply register to that vendor interface. This would avoid having yet another patch to support into ACK (the \"cpu pause\" feature already had to diverged from android-mainline) and leave the choice to any other vendor to handle the feature the way they want.",
      "revId": "fcda8540b9d5e1222433dd049660f2609c120be2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "34321501_fadf6724",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1761165
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-05T00:22:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, this can be implemented in a module, and I had an implementation that did it in that way.  \n\nThe team wanted this in ACK, because it is a better solution.  What if there is yet another module that is developed, perhaps downstream from QC, which uses the pause interface directly, as they certainly are allowed to do?  Under those circumstances, you might have OEM code that will fail sometimes. In other words, those entities will be trying to pause (or unpause) a CPU, and fighting other modules like thermal and core-ctl.\n\nWorst case, you could have a system that is unpausing a thermal-paused CPU, negating thermal\u0027s goal of reducing the CPU\u0027s temperature. With ref-counting in pause_cpus()/resume_cpus(), this won\u0027t happen.",
      "parentUuid": "bff40832_c2678b2f",
      "revId": "fcda8540b9d5e1222433dd049660f2609c120be2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ea6ba0cb_03a43728",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1569742
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-09T09:19:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tend to agree with Vincent on this one. If OEMs want to use the Pause feature, it\u0027s on them to do it correctly. GKI already follows that logic -- partners can attach to vendor hooks if they want, but it\u0027s their responsibility to not break their product. I would argue the same applies here, so I\u0027m not convinced yet we need this patch in ACK.",
      "parentUuid": "34321501_fadf6724",
      "revId": "fcda8540b9d5e1222433dd049660f2609c120be2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
